A||||5||Smoooooth GT||Dist. Module question:||||5||
Z||000000||Smoooooth GT||12-29-2001||12:16 PM||||I replaced the module in the dist. yesterday.. My car fired right up.. My question is:  What would cause it to go out?? Should I check anything else?? Would something make it go bad or will it do it on it's own?? Thank's for any input!! Steve<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<P>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, side scoop's, sail scoop's, ZR-1 hood scoop, decklid scoop, BMW Z~3 vent's, 308 headlight cover's, Custom front and rear fascia's...smooooth!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||12-29-2001||12:20 PM||||Usually they die on there own from heat. The fiero engine compartment is not kind to the electronic parts of the car. Just make sure you have some heat sink grease between the module and the Dist. for cooling.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||12-29-2001||12:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B>Usually they die on there own from heat. The fiero engine compartment is not kind to the electronic parts of the car. Just make sure you have some heat sink grease between the module and the Dist. for cooling.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Where would I find that??  Regular part's store??  Thank's, I'm glad I probably don't have to track anything else down!! <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<P>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, side scoop's, sail scoop's, ZR-1 hood scoop, decklid scoop, BMW Z~3 vent's, 308 headlight cover's, Custom front and rear fascia's...smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-29-2001||01:27 PM||||Heat sink gease or di-electric grease can be found in any auto parts store.  Ususally in a bubble pack in the electronic parts area.  The stuff I found was in a Pep Boys, the tube about half the size of your little finger  You don't need much.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-29-2001||01:36 PM||||Old Lar... Thank's for the infomation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
